       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Acetaminophen 9,000 mg/day has no recognized therapeutic use. It is in the range that causes hepatotoxicity and could seriously harm the patient. Normal liver function and a 70 kg weight don't change that. You also didn't give a clinical rationale, and I can't verify one from here.\n\nI can enter any of these now:\n- Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO four times daily (4 g/day, the usual ceiling)\n- A different analgesic or multimodal regimen, if pain control is the issue\n\nIf you think a nonstandard dose is warranted, for example under toxicology guidance, that should go through pharmacy and your institution's override process, not through me. If the dose was a typo, such as 300 mg or 1,000 mg, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
